{"case": "short-code", "summary": {"case": "short-code", "ok": true, "err": null, "ttft_s": 0.784, "total_s": 6.816, "prompt_tokens": 29, "reused_tokens": 0, "read_tokens": 29, "generated_tokens": 256, "prompt_tps": 41.4, "prompt_tps_source": "engine", "decode_tps": 42.3, "decode_tps_source": "engine", "prompt_ms": 700.1, "decode_ms": 6052.5, "drafts_offered": 184, "drafts_accepted": 146}, "result": {"first": 0.7836115000245627, "total": 6.815901709022, "text": "# LRU Cache Implementation Using `OrderedDict`\n\n## Implementation\n\n```python\nfrom collections import OrderedDict\n\n\nclass LRUCache:\n    \"\"\"\n    Least Recently Used (LRU) cache with O(1) get/put operations.\n    \n    Uses an OrderedDict to maintain insertion order, where the most recently\n    used item is moved to the end on every access. When capacity is exceeded,\n    the least recently used item (at the front) is evicted.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, capacity: int):\n        if capacity <= 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"Capacity must be a positive integer\")\n        self.capacity = capacity\n        # OrderedDict maintains insertion order; we use it as our backing store.\n        # Keys are cache keys, values are cached values.\n        self._cache = OrderedDict()\n\n    def get(self, key):\n        \"\"\"\n        Retrieve value for `key`. Returns None if not present.\n        On a hit, the accessed item is moved to the end (most recently used).\n        \"\"\"\n        if key not in self._cache:\n            return None\n        # Move the accessed key to the end → marks it as most recently used\n", "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 29, "completion_tokens": 256, "total_tokens": 285, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}}, "timings": {"cache_n": 0, "prompt_n": 29, "prompt_ms": 700.1, "prompt_per_token_ms": 24.141, "prompt_per_second": 41.4, "predicted_n": 256, "predicted_ms": 6052.5, "predicted_per_token_ms": 23.643, "predicted_per_second": 42.3, "draft_n": 184, "draft_n_accepted": 146}, "err": null, "pieces": 231}}
